<?xml version='1.0' encoding='windows-1252'?>

<!--
  ============================================================================
  THIS FILE IS HAND-EDITED. Three changes, each marked HAND-EDITED below:

    * a `ProgramMenuFolder` directory,
    * a Start Menu shortcut nested in the binary's `File`,
    * the product icon, enabled and pointed at `wix\Product.ico`.

  It started as a cargo-dist template, and dist rewrites its templates on every
  `dist generate` — worse, `dist plan` *fails* on one it does not recognise,
  which would take every release down with it. `allow-dirty = ["msi"]` in
  dist-workspace.toml is what hands ownership over; without it none of the
  above survives, and the release workflow stops working.

  The `msi-customisation` step in .github/workflows/ci.yml checks the edits are
  still here, in case that config line is ever dropped.
  ============================================================================
-->

